diff --git a/Documentation/git-betterleaks--diff-engine.adoc b/Documentation/git-betterleaks--diff-engine.adoc
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b10a46cf3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/git-betterleaks--diff-engine.adoc
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+git-betterleaks--diff-engine(1)
+=================================
+
+NAME
+----
+git-betterleaks--diff-engine - experimental typed history-diff helper
+
+SYNOPSIS
+--------
+[verse]
+'git betterleaks--diff-engine' --protocol=1
+
+DESCRIPTION
+-----------
+This experimental plumbing command serves sequential, length-prefixed binary
+requests on standard input and writes typed commit, file, and added-hunk
+records on standard output. It is an internal Betterleaks performance
+experiment, not a stable Git interface.
+
+Protocol version 1 uses big-endian integers, raw SHA-1 or SHA-256 object IDs,
+and a 16 MiB frame bound. Requests use `BGIN` frames and the process is closed
+with `QUIT`. Responses are nested `CMIT`, `FBEG`, hunk, and matching end
+frames, terminated by `BEND`. Large hunks use `HBGN`, `HADD`, and `HEND`.
+`ERRO` is terminal. Before `HELO`, an unsupported repository capability is
+reported as error kind 5 with batch ID zero, then the helper exits cleanly.
+
+The diff profile is fixed to root commits, no merge diffs, `-U0`, `-M50%`,
+the A/M/R production filter, Myers with the indent heuristic, textconv, and no
+external diff. The command disables replace objects. Protocol stdout must not
+be used for diagnostics.
+
+GIT
+---
+Part of the linkgit:git[1] suite
